## How to Define API Routes
In TanStack Start, API routes are a feature for creating server-side endpoints.
These can be used for tasks such as form submissions and user authentication.
They are defined within the `./app/routes/api` directory of your project and are automatically handled by the TanStack Start server.
By default, they are prefixed with `/api`.
This base path can be customized by changing `apiBase` in the configuration.
...
